      "q": "1. Mention the advantages of selecting pea plants for experiments by Mendel.",
      "a": "The pea plant (Pisum sativum) was chosen by Mendel for the following reasons:\n\nThe pea is an annual plant with a brief growing season. As a result, the findings can be achieved in a short amount of time.\n\nPea has seven distinct features with easily distinguishable traits such as tall and short stature, round and yellow seeds, and so on.\n\nSelf-pollination and cross-pollination are both viable options for pea propagation. Mendel was able to create pure lines as well as carry out various crosses between plants with contrasting features as a result of this.\n\nEach generation of the pea plant produces a great number of seeds. As a result, it can provide a vast volume of data that can be statistically more reliably analyzed, for example.\n\nStartFragment"
