      "q": "13: What is DNA Fingerprinting? Mention its Application.",
      "a": "The technique which is used to identify and analyse the variation in DNA in every individual is known as DNA fingerprinting.\n\nThe various applications of DNA fingerprinting are as follow:\n\nIn forensic science, it is used for identifying potential crime suspects.\n\nIt is used for finding out paternity and family relationships.\n\nIt is used for the identification and protection of commercial crop varieties and livestock.\n\nIt is used to find out the evolutionary relationship and linkage between the various organisms."
